    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Terrestrial carbon cycle",
    "problem": "Land carbon cycle models disagree on the primary environmental drivers controlling terrestrial carbon uptake, with compensatory effects between sensitivities to CO\u2082 and climate undermining the reliability of future carbon-climate feedback predictions.",
    "method": "To address large uncertainties in carbon-climate feedback predictions, the authors suggest the modeling community prioritize a probabilistic multi-model ensemble approach, akin to weather forecasting, to generate more robust projections of the terrestrial carbon cycle.",
    "task": "The task is to use an ensemble of land models to quantify uncertainty in the response of the terrestrial carbon sink to key environmental drivers and to understand how disagreement among models undermines the predictability of future carbon-climate feedbacks.",
